Z||000013||william_thorniii||10-26-2000||01:28 PM||||88,<P>I think you slightly misunderstood the nature of my post.  I was not implying that the Fiero was not a sports car.  However if you would like to get technical on the subject, I can assure you that the spoiler on a Fiero is non-functional and is merely for looks.  To some of us that is pure hypocrisy.<P>Furthermore, it was not my intent to tell Dave not to put a spoiler on the car.  He can do with his property as he wishes.  I was merely suggesting that to some folks (screwy as it may seem) might find the car more attractive the way it is.  To me the spoiler clutters the pure lines of the fastbacks hind quarters.  In fact, I would not buy a fastback with a spoiler.  Also it is of importance that Dave is a re-seller.  This car is effectually not Daves (for long at least) and many would feel an original car be better left original.  <P>FD,<P>Once again... I suggest your shall from henceforth become Super Dave!<P>Thanks for taking us freaks (myself and Stimpy) into consideration.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000014||mrfixit58||10-26-2000||03:12 PM||||Another vote for the original wing delete. I've got the blue 87 GT w/o the wing and the longer I own it, the more I like it w/o the wing. You just don't see too may GTs w/o wings... especially black ones. I like being unique. But, to each his own.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
